# chip_tracks, with the H ORIGINS PLACED FOR A MIRRORED LAYOUT.
#
# The PATTERNS here are byte-identical to chip_tracks.buda — same stack, same
# widths, same 10 signals per period, same periods, same overheads, same 504
# grid.  THE ONLY DIFFERENCE IS THREE H ORIGINS: M4 -199, M6 -403.5, M8 -802
# (against -200 / -400 / -800).  Everything else in this file is a copy.
#
# WHY A SEPARATE FILE.  A flipped instance's routing is its reference's routing
# reflected about the instance's own centreline, so the layer's pattern must be
# invariant under that reflection — the centreline must land on a reflection
# AXIS of the pattern.  Two things are needed and they are independent:
#
#   1. the pattern must HAVE axes at all -- it must be a palindrome.  That is
#      now true in chip_tracks.buda itself (each rail centred in its gap), so
#      this file inherits it and no longer has to change any slot.
#   2. the ORIGIN must put an axis ON the instance centrelines.  That is what
#      is left, and it is placement-specific, which is why it cannot live in
#      the shared file: chip_stack's three flipped instances sit at centres
#      8694 / 10710 / 12222, all differing by multiples of 504, so one origin
#      per layer serves all three -- but they are THIS design's centres.
#
# The condition is  instance_centre - origin == axis  (mod period/2), and each
# layer's axis sits at the power-rail centre (rail/2), so:
#
#   layer  period  axis (mod p/2)  origin  shift
#   M2       18     1  (mod 9)     -100    none needed
#   M4       18     1  (mod 9)     -199    +1
#   M6       24     1.5 (mod 12)   -403.5  -3.5
#   M8       56     4  (mod 28)    -802    -2
#
# M10 CANNOT be satisfied and does not need to be: its half period 37 does not
# divide 504, so the three flipped centres fall on three different residues and
# no single origin serves them.  That is precisely why `reserve_top_layers 2`
# caps cells at M9 — the grid is the LCM over the layers the CELLS use, and M10
# is not one of them.
#
# The V origins are the shared file's: an upside-down flip maps y -> 2d-y and
# leaves x alone, so vertical tracks take no part in this.
def_layer  2 M2  H LOW 58.33
def_layer  3 M3  V LOW 58.33
def_layer  4 M4  H TOP 58.33
def_layer  5 M5  V TOP 58.33
def_layer  6 M6  H TOP 68.75
def_layer  7 M7  V TOP 58.33
def_layer  8 M8  H TOP 57.59
def_layer  9 M9  V TOP 57.59
def_layer 10 M10 H TOP 56.08
def_layer 11 M11 V TOP 56.08

# H layers — symmetric units (rail centred in its gap), periods unchanged.
def_track_pattern 2  -100   POWER 2 0.875  SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.875  GROUND 2 0.875  SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.875
def_track_pattern 4  -199   POWER 2 0.875  SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.875  GROUND 2 0.875  SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.875
def_track_pattern 6  -403.5 POWER 3 1.125  SIGNAL 0.75 0.75 SIGNAL 0.75 0.75 SIGNAL 0.75 0.75 SIGNAL 0.75 0.75 SIGNAL 0.75 1.125  GROUND 3 1.125  SIGNAL 0.75 0.75 SIGNAL 0.75 0.75 SIGNAL 0.75 0.75 SIGNAL 0.75 0.75 SIGNAL 0.75 1.125
def_track_pattern 8  -802   POWER 8 1.6875  SIGNAL 2.375 1.1875 SIGNAL 2.375 1.1875 SIGNAL 2.375 1.1875 SIGNAL 2.375 1.1875 SIGNAL 2.375 1.6875  GROUND 8 1.6875  SIGNAL 2.375 1.1875 SIGNAL 2.375 1.1875 SIGNAL 2.375 1.1875 SIGNAL 2.375 1.1875 SIGNAL 2.375 1.6875
def_track_pattern 10 -1200  POWER 10 2.125  SIGNAL 3.25 1.625 SIGNAL 3.25 1.625 SIGNAL 3.25 1.625 SIGNAL 3.25 1.625 SIGNAL 3.25 2.125  GROUND 10 2.125  SIGNAL 3.25 1.625 SIGNAL 3.25 1.625 SIGNAL 3.25 1.625 SIGNAL 3.25 1.625 SIGNAL 3.25 2.125

# V layers — unchanged from chip_tracks.buda (a y-flip does not move them).
def_track_pattern 3  0      POWER 2 0.875  SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.875  GROUND 2 0.875  SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.875
def_track_pattern 5  0      POWER 2 0.875  SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.875  GROUND 2 0.875  SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.875
def_track_pattern 7  -600   POWER 6 1.0625  SIGNAL 1.625 0.8125 SIGNAL 1.625 0.8125 SIGNAL 1.625 0.8125 SIGNAL 1.625 0.8125 SIGNAL 1.625 1.0625  GROUND 6 1.0625  SIGNAL 1.625 0.8125 SIGNAL 1.625 0.8125 SIGNAL 1.625 0.8125 SIGNAL 1.625 0.8125 SIGNAL 1.625 1.0625
def_track_pattern 9  -1000  POWER 8 1.6875  SIGNAL 2.375 1.1875 SIGNAL 2.375 1.1875 SIGNAL 2.375 1.1875 SIGNAL 2.375 1.1875 SIGNAL 2.375 1.6875  GROUND 8 1.6875  SIGNAL 2.375 1.1875 SIGNAL 2.375 1.1875 SIGNAL 2.375 1.1875 SIGNAL 2.375 1.1875 SIGNAL 2.375 1.6875
def_track_pattern 11 -1400  POWER 10 2.125  SIGNAL 3.25 1.625 SIGNAL 3.25 1.625 SIGNAL 3.25 1.625 SIGNAL 3.25 1.625 SIGNAL 3.25 2.125  GROUND 10 2.125  SIGNAL 3.25 1.625 SIGNAL 3.25 1.625 SIGNAL 3.25 1.625 SIGNAL 3.25 1.625 SIGNAL 3.25 2.125

report_overhead
